---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site collects and why.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated October 2026</p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, which counts page views without cookies and without identifying you, and
      <strong>Google Analytics</strong>, which shows which pages and features people use: for example, which gallery filters are popular or
      whether the contact form is working.
    </p>
    <p>
      Outside the EU/EEA, the UK, and Switzerland, Google Analytics stores a first-party cookie (<code>_ga</code>) to tell visits apart. Inside
      those regions it sets no cookies and sends only anonymous, cookieless measurements. Google Analytics doesn't store IP addresses, and
      advertising features, Google signals, and ad personalization are turned off everywhere. Nothing is sold or used for ads.
    </p>
    <p>
      To opt out of Google Analytics on every site, use Google's
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">opt-out browser add-on</a>, or block cookies for this site in your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact form</h2>
    <p>
      What you type into the contact form (name, email, topic, subject, message) is emailed to me so I can reply, and isn't used for anything
      else. Cloudflare Turnstile checks that the sender isn't a bot. Messages are delivered through Resend.
    </p>

    <h2>Embedded videos</h2>
    <p>
      YouTube and Instagram videos only load after you click play. Once loaded, they're served by those companies under their own privacy
      policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>Use the <a href="/about/#contact">contact form</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  article { display: grid; gap: 12px; padding: 12px 0 24px; }
  h2 { margin-top: 18px; }
  code { font-size: 0.9em; background: var(--chip); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); }
</style>
